      "side": 1,
      "message": "This algorithm will be very wasteful when there are lots of projects in a tree because it will do a query per project. It would be better to change this to be 1 query per level in the hierarchy. For example, given the project_id passed in to the method get its children. Then take that list of children and get all of their children in one query like: (query.filter(Project.id.in_(children_ids)). Do this until you have gotten to the leaf nodes in the tree.\n\nThere is one complication in that you may get too many children at a level to do the in_ method and may have to break it up. With a small hierarchy this would cut the queries in half. With a larger hierarchy it would be even better.",
      "revId": "20680f50b36f0c80bb2750b0407269a7408071fe",
